.TH "wmmenugen" "1" "16 May 2015"
.SH "NAME"
\fBwmmenugen\fR \- Window Maker PropList menu generator
.PP
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B wmmenugen
.RI [ options ...]
.BI \-parser= <name>
.IR fspec " [" fspec "...]"
.BI \fR[\fP\-parser= <name>
.IR fspec " [" fspec "...]...]"
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.B wmmenugen
generates a menu in the
.I PropList
format for Window Maker from the input file
.IR fspec .
In the case where
.I fspec
is a directory instead of a file, then
.B wmmenugen
will read all the files present in the hierarchy of this directory.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
.B \-\-applications
Generate a categorized menu from installed desktop entries. Searches
XDG_DATA_HOME/applications and XDG_DATA_DIRS/applications, including nested
directories, with user overrides and hidden entries taking precedence.
Defaults are ~/.local/share, /usr/local/share and /usr/share.
.TP
.BI \-\-category " CATEGORY"
Include only entries in this desktop-entry category, as a flat submenu.
Examples: Network, TerminalEmulator, Development and Office.
Other selects entries without a recognized main category.
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
print a help message with the list of options
.TP
.BI \-\-icon-size " PIXELS"
Preferred icon size, from 1 to 512 pixels (default 24). The nearest available
theme size is chosen and Window Maker scales the image to its menu row.
.TP
.BI \-\-icon-theme " THEME"
Override the icon theme. By default, gtk-icon-theme-name is read from GTK 4
then GTK 3 settings.ini under XDG_CONFIG_HOME, then ~/.gtkrc-2.0.
Theme inheritance and hicolor are searched before unthemed icons and pixmaps.
XDG data directories and ~/.icons are searched, with user icons taking precedence.
PNG and XPM are supported; SVG icons require an ImageMagick-enabled build.
.TP
.BI \-\-launch " DESKTOP-ID"
Launch a desktop file ID or absolute desktop filename using GIO. This preserves
desktop-entry argument quoting and field codes, Terminal, Path and D-Bus activation,
rather than interpreting Exec as a shell command.
.TP
.B \-\-no-icons
Omit icons from the Applications menu.
.TP
.B \-parser
specify the format of the file to be parsed
.TP
.B \-\-version
print the version of Window Maker from which the program comes
.SH "PARSERS"
.B wmmenugen
supports these file formats for input files:
.TP
.I wmconfig
the format of the menu generation tool for X of the same name
.TP
.I xdg
the format of the menu specification as defined by the
.I FreeDesktop
standard, currently at version 1.1
.SH "APPLICATIONS MENUS"
The Applications item in WPrefs creates a dynamic submenu, either the whole tree
or one selected category. Names are localized. NoDisplay, Hidden, OnlyShowIn,
NotShowIn and TryExec are honored. XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP is used for visibility;
if unset, WindowMaker is assumed.
.PP
The whole tree uses the standard main categories, with terminal emulators grouped
under Terminals. It is not an implementation of distribution-specific .menu XML
layouts or merge rules.
.PP
Example WMRootMenu entries:
.nf
("Applications", APPLICATIONS_MENU)
("Network", APPLICATIONS_MENU, Network)
("Terminals", APPLICATIONS_MENU, TerminalEmulator)
.fi
.PP
Standalone generation: wmmenugen --applications --category Network
.PP
Generation runs when the submenu is opened, so application installations,
removals, user overrides and icon-theme changes appear without restarting.
Theme metadata, directory listings and icon results are cached within each
invocation; there is no stale persistent menu cache.
An empty category displays a disabled "(No items)" entry.
.PP
Applications mode requires GIO support at build time. Legacy parsers and
wmgenmenu remain available without it.
.PP
Desktop entries also expose GenericName, Comment, Keywords, MIME associations
and application Actions. These are useful for future search, tooltips and
per-application action menus; they are not currently displayed in this menu.
.SH "RETURN VALUE"
The exit status from the
.B wmmenugen
command provides information for the caller:
.TP
.B 0
when the
.I PropList
menu was successfully generated on
.IR stdout .
.TP
.B 1
when a
.I fspec
caused a problem (non readable file, ...)
.TP
.B 2
the arguments of the command line where not recognised
.TP
.B 3
the program met an unexpected menu structure;
you probably want to look at the section
.B BUGS
below.
.SH "BUGS"
If you get the exit status
.B 3
with the unclear error message about
.IR "unprocessed levels on the stack" ,
you encountered a limitation of
.BR wmmenugen .
It would be a good idea to prepare an archive with the files incriminated and submit them to the
mailing list (wmaker-dev@googlegroups.com) with you command line, so the team can work on
improving the behaviour of the program on this case.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR wmgenmenu (1),
the tool to generate a default menu
.PP
the
.I Wmconfig
program can be found at:
<http://www.arrishq.net/index.html>
.PP
the
.I xdg
specification can be found at:
<http://standards.freedesktop.org/menu-spec/menu-spec-1.1.html>
